Z||000002||Mach10||07-12-2001||09:16 PM||||You'd have to start by building a model on a model Fiero. Then you'd have to digitize it, then find someone to make some moulds based on your model. I was going to design one myself, but my AutoCAD skills aren't up to par yet. What I'd REALLY like is some plastic models to play with. I wonder if anyone makes 'em?||||reg||9
Z||000003||cadaver||07-12-2001||09:22 PM||||Hey Mach what do you think they did back in the day before computers. Autocad is bascially a new thing. Try reading a scale.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||07-13-2001||12:23 AM||||We had a guy that said he was interested in funding just such a thing but never found anyone that was capable or interested in doing the work..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||07-13-2001||02:05 AM||||Cadaver: FYI, I *CAN* read a scale...<BR>There! 179 lbs. See?<P>You do know that sending out a cad drawing of what you want will shave thousands of dollars (read hours) off the production price, as well as being easier to edit? What I'd like is a plastic model of a fiero, a coupld of pictures, and some gelled resin. Then I'll have a scale model of an '89 Fiero. Bung it into a digitizer, wait the requisite 15 hours to render, break the model into panels per measured specs, and ship it to one of the plastic companies to make the moulds. If you already have the design work done, and in a language that the mills can understand, you can have that set of moulds for a couple of grand, much less than the 10k we're talking about earlier. Of course, I could make it even cheaper with a donor car, a donor model, and LOT of fiberglass to make a prototype of. I'd like to do that, but at the moment, I don't have the time, nor the shop tools. Give me 6 months, and I'll re-assess the feasibility. <P>I'd make a prototype "mule" for the cost of the Fiero, cost of raw materials, plus the installation and purchase of a 3800 S-II SC motor into my current '86. Really! I don't have a life, so I wouldn't be missing much.<BR>The biggest limiting factor is the photos. Do we have one of front, back, and both sides?<BR>Would GM sue me if they saw it?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||07-13-2001||02:42 AM||||Oh, my god. I've just figured out how to do it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>It *IS* possible, and only some modifications to the chassis are necessary. EUREKA!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000007||rc5star||07-13-2001||07:42 AM||||Hey Mach10, if you need anyone to work some cad files let me know. I have full access to Catia and Unigraphics. I have seen some of the cad files after they have ran a scan over the clay model of a new car and they are filled with millions of points that have to be made into panels. I have never worked on the prosses of changing all the points to a file that a shop could use to make body panels but I know how its done. So if any of my cad skills can help just let me know.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mach10||07-13-2001||10:20 AM||||Actually, this method would come in 2 parts. First on a plastic model, then on an empty chassis. The hardest bit will be getting the moulded rear panel done up.||||reg||7
Z||000009||Mach10||07-14-2001||08:18 PM||||SWEET! I found all the pictures that I need. Now, if only I had the startup capital to take on this adventure   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Anyone with a plastic mill wanna chip in?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I'm going to start on this project out of general interest, and I have a pretty good idea of how to finish it. Of course, with my schedule, it is going to take a while, but hey, I need another hobby   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>BTW: Cadaver: Thanks for the idea!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||7
