Z||000016||ray b||07-16-2001||11:35 PM||||you could do it like a boat is done<BR>make a buck [full size form] in clay, wax<BR>or plaster then mold off that.<BR>but 100's of hours cleaning up the mold<BR>is the big cost factor to make it super smooth.<BR>pro mold makers will charge way tooo much<BR>to use autocad buck forming mold.<BR>carbon fiber or kevar could be used[lite]<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000017||Mach10||07-17-2001||02:15 AM||||As always, Ray, your input is much enjoyed.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I've thought of that, but I need a scale to work off of, or else it's just eyeballing. On a small scale that'll work, but if I'm off 0.1 mm on the model, that'd be almost an inch off on the final product. Unacceptable. Now, if I got numbers, then it's possible.<P>Not a bad idea though. I just kinda want to get the thing on paper with some hard numbers before starting anything concrete(enduraflex   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>I'm 99% confident that I can have blueprints by September. As for having moulds done, I would need "investors" or at least people willing to buy panels. At the moment, I'm not in it for money, but rather as an interest thing. The *sweetest* thing that could happen is one of the larger Fiero stores buying into the project. Not too likely to happen. <P>Hey, like I said! I'll do ALL of the grunt work in exchange for a complete (labor incl.) 3800SC swap into my '86   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Edit:<BR>I need a photo, sorry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> That's the right angle, though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||6
