Z||000034||AusFiero||07-20-2001||09:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TI_3VOM:<BR>[Bgo to members.nbci.com/WPFC/89discovery.html ...pic of the '89 Fiero prototypes (some still exist)<BR>[B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 3 in the Detroit holding yard got crushed before easter as did everything else in the yard. Which does still leave the grey one and red one used in promotions and show. Jim Mattison of Pontiac Historical Services doubts they even exist anymore. Jim was here at easter for our nats and told us about their demise.<P>Although I think the grey one used for promotions was one of the crushed ones.<P>So maybe somewhere the red one is still hiding. If it is,  Pontiac won't tell Historical Services about it. <P>The pictures on that website were taken by a personal friend of mine Dave Clee who owns Ponti-World Australa. I have been onto him to get the large high resolution originals but he has not had time to look through his 100s of discs of photos. <P>Will try again when he gets back from the states in a week or 2 as he is currently over there doing his duties as a director of POCI.<P>That holding yard is now empty waiting a whole new breed of cars to crush in the future.<P>I knew I shouldn't have missed that trip but I was building my new house and cancelled out.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000035||TI_3VOM||07-21-2001||03:43 PM||||...(in the immortal words of Eric Cartman)<P>SONOFAB***H!!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>||||reg||9
Z||000036||Mach10||07-21-2001||06:27 PM||||Aus: If you could scam me some nice high-res pics, the outcome would be so much better    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I need a side view (both would be prefereable) a front view, and a rear-view. Top-down would be nice but not critical.<P>Oh, BTW, my design will be off the gray 89 as I have found the most complete photos of this one, and as you can see above, the frame is very close to the 84-88 frame. I will be getting some measurements done in the next while, and will start looking into how far the 84-88 frame needs to be extended. That's what I need the photo of the frame for. Of course, if anyone wants to donate an un-wrecked but otherwise dead 84 (no motor/trans needed. Just wheels.) to the cause, I could use that also.<P>If only I could get a guarantee of return off this, since I will have to spend money that'd be better spent on my own 86  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>don't suppose anyone has a line on raw materials and wants to "help" me out? I need lots of resin, and lots of 'glass...<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-21-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000037||TI_3VOM||07-21-2001||07:00 PM||||...from the articles I've read, there should be hardly any altercations made to the space frame. Same wheelbase, same ('88) suspension, same space frame (albeit in aluminum and glued, not welded, together). Looks like this could be pretty much a bolt on. The only problem that I could see is what will be used for the headlights (wider than the 84-88 Fiero), and how to produce/mount those transparent fastback sail panels/surround. <P>P.S. also try to get a hold of the April '94 issue of Collectible Automobile. Great article and pics.||||reg||5
Z||000038||Mach10||07-21-2001||09:01 PM||||I'll be dealing with the ancilliaries later. Right now, I'm more concerned about the frame modifications. The rear has to be extended to fit what appears to be an enlarged trunk, although the wheelbase stays the same. I have a source on who can do me the rear sail panels, so I'm not working on that right now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The only thing I really need is money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000039||AusFiero||07-22-2001||02:58 AM||||I will definately hassle him up again Mach 10 because those photos are only 3 of about 20 he took. I seen them all when he originally got home from the trip. I spoke to his wife today actually. He is LA at the moment and is flying home on Wednesday. I will go visit him next weekend and grab a pile of discs myself to start searching if he don't have the time. I know he wont as he is very busy.<P>He has interior pictures, front, rear, engine bay and a few different angles.<P>Also a handly little tip straight from the designers that does make a kit feasible. The frames under those cars were unmolested 88 frames with extensions to make it all look right. Basically a bigger accident absorbion area.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
